{
  "_source": "CLAUDE.md §54 TESTING and §55 ADVERSARIAL TESTS. The 29 invariants and the 52 adversarial cases (11 Data, 7 Methodology, 7 Decision, 11 News, 8 Research, 8 Execution) below are the spec's own lists, in its order and wording. scripts/tests/test_coverage.py parses them back out of CLAUDE.md, so a new bullet in either section fails the build.",
  "_reader": "scripts/test_coverage.py is the ONE reader. Every citation is `path::test_function`, and the checker RESOLVES each one -- a citation pointing at a test that no longer exists fails, which is what stops this file becoming a list of good intentions.",
  "_why_this_exists": "§54 and §55 are the two sections a repository cannot self-report on. Both had been audited by hand -- 18 of 29 and 14 of 38 -- and a hand audit is accurate on the day it is written and never again. Making the audit a registry with resolvable citations turns 'are the invariants tested?' into a question the suite answers about itself.",
  "_uncovered_is_a_value": "A case with no test must declare `covered: false` AND a reason. 'Not yet written' and 'cannot be written because the feature does not exist' are different facts, and only the first is a to-do. The checker refuses an uncovered entry with no reason.",
